#=============================================================================
# RF Receiver Identity Map (RF Event Fusion — see DOCs/RF-EVENT-FUSION.md)
#=============================================================================
#
# FORMAT:
#   rx-XXXXXX : friendly-name : location : notes
#
# The receiver identity is derived from ESP.getChipId() and baked into the
# firmware as the literal string "rx-XXXXXX" (field 4 of the RF message). It is
# immutable and unique per board, so:
#   - friendly names live HERE, server-side, and are never baked into firmware;
#   - a reflashed/overtaken board can never impersonate another receiver;
#   - the SAME firmware image fits every receiver (no per-unit build).
#
# The boot banner prints the id, and every RF message carries it in field 4, so
# you can always map a freshly flashed board without guessing.
#
# NOTE: consumed by buttonPressReceiver.sh since 2026-10-18 — it translates the
# receiver id carried in field 4 of every RF message into the friendly name
# used in the fusion log ("FUSED ... via=rf-fridge@0ms,..."). Keep it updated
# whenever a receiver is flashed or moved.
#
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# chipID (rx-XXXXXX) : friendly-name : location : notes
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

rx-241002 : rf-fridge : kitchen (by the refrigerator) : D1 mini + RXB6 @3.3V, coiled antenna as shipped — installed 2026-10-18 to replace the kitchen/fridge nodeMCU. On v2.2 since 2026-10-18: its OTA listener was wedged (DOCs §7 "OTA") so it was reflashed over USB from the Mac; hello framing wire-verified single-segment.

rx-55d68f : rf-laundry : laundry : nodeMCU-1 reinstalled 2026-10-18 (was running the v1 "connection YESSS, pin D2/GPIO4" sketch), flashed to v2 then OTA'd to v2.2 the same day, framing wire-verified. v1 source recovered from git 196e049^ ; pre-flash full-flash backup md5 6e72b82a9f3ae1a050d8b9d81c199a83

rx-058ef5 : rf-central : corridor / hallway (central) : nodeMCU-0 — **v2.2 since 2026-10-19** (USB-flashed from the Mac; v1 had no OTA at all, so USB was mandatory). Id CONFIRMED by the boot banner (`Version: 2.2 (RF Event Fusion)   id: rx-058ef5`, MAC ec:fa:bc:05:8e:f5, matching the prediction), SNTP synced, hello framing wire-verified single-segment (`len=21 b'rx-058ef5 connected\r\n'`). Hears nearly every remote (master corridor, Nicolò, kitchen, bilocale) → central placement. **Reinstalled in the corridor 2026-10-19 → fleet complete → fusion armed the same day** (`FUSION_WINDOW_MS=1500`, `FUSION_ENABLED=1`): its first field presses produced the first `n=3` groups (see DOCs/RF-EVENT-FUSION.md §4 step 4).
